  "scientific_conclusion": "The frozen homogeneous source update satisfies the independent raw-moment linear-relaxation identity to about 2.33e-16 for every arm. The retained clipped active target nevertheless injects material state and heat-flux-law errors, reaching 3.6041% and 5.7487%, respectively, across the five preregistered states. The unclipped paper target and bounded-conservative diagnostic reduce those errors to the 1e-9 and 1e-8 scale, but the bounded-conservative maxima exceed the unchanged strict 1e-9 and 1e-8 thresholds by 4.89e-10 and 3.35e-9. The strict blocker is retained; neither diagnostic replaces the active solver, failed parameters are not retuned, and the failed MUSCL endpoint remains negative.",
